Let an outer text system ask which font database face a FontId is.

What: add `CosmicTextSystem::font_database_id(FontId) -> Option<fontdb::ID>` in gpui_wgpu. Read-only, no
behaviour change.

Why: Parallax's Android text system wraps CosmicTextSystem and has Android draw colour emoji itself (swash
cannot paint COLRv1, the only emoji font on API 33+ images without NotoColorEmojiLegacy.ttf). It must know
which shaped runs come from the system emoji files listed in fonts.xml (NotoColorEmoji.ttf and the separate
flags font), including the fallback faces cosmic-text picks during layout. A `FontId` is an index into
CosmicTextSystem's private font list, so without this the wrapper cannot map a run back to its file.
`check_is_known_emoji_font` matches the PostScript name `NotoColorEmoji` only and misses the flags font.

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

